                      (1/cmds/format.asm):00001         ********************************************************************
                      (1/cmds/format.asm):00002         * Format - RBF Disk format program
                      (1/cmds/format.asm):00003         *
                      (1/cmds/format.asm):00004         * Notes:
                      (1/cmds/format.asm):00005         *   1. If the TYP.DSQ bit in IT.TYP is clear, then the total number
                      (1/cmds/format.asm):00006         *      of sectors is NOT multiplied by the bytes per sector.  This
                      (1/cmds/format.asm):00007         *      means that descriptors using partition offsets will need to
                      (1/cmds/format.asm):00008         *      fill IT.CYL, IT.SID and IT.SCT with values that reflect the
                      (1/cmds/format.asm):00009         *      number of 256 byte sectors on the disk.
                      (1/cmds/format.asm):00010         *
                      (1/cmds/format.asm):00011         * Edt/Rev  YYYY/MM/DD  Modified by
                      (1/cmds/format.asm):00012         * Comment
                      (1/cmds/format.asm):00013         * ------------------------------------------------------------------
                      (1/cmds/format.asm):00014         *  22      ????/??/??
                      (1/cmds/format.asm):00015         * From Tandy OS-9 Level Two VR 02.00.01.
                      (1/cmds/format.asm):00016         *
                      (1/cmds/format.asm):00017         *  23      2003/01/06  JC
                      (1/cmds/format.asm):00018         * Format incorrect/clusters summary: now, specifying cluster size works.
                      (1/cmds/format.asm):00019         * Fixed bug where format showed an improper number of sectors formatted
                      (1/cmds/format.asm):00020         * at the summary if the number of sectors was a large number.
                      (1/cmds/format.asm):00021         * This was most notable when formatting large disks, such as hard drives.
                      (1/cmds/format.asm):00022         *
                      (1/cmds/format.asm):00023         *  24      2004/07/20  Boisy G. Pitre
                      (1/cmds/format.asm):00024         * Revamped to display summary similar to OS-9/68K. Also, format now
                      (1/cmds/format.asm):00025         * checks the TYPH.DSQ bit in order to query the drive for its size.
                      (1/cmds/format.asm):00026         * A rolling track counter that stays on the same line is now used
                      (1/cmds/format.asm):00027         * instead of the scrolling track counter, and 4 byte track numbers
                      (1/cmds/format.asm):00028         * are now shown instead of 3 byte track numbers.
                      (1/cmds/format.asm):00029         * Also, if a cluster size is not specified on the command line,
                      (1/cmds/format.asm):00030         * the best one is automatically calculated.
                      (1/cmds/format.asm):00031         *
                      (1/cmds/format.asm):00032         *       2005-10-25  P.Harvey-Smith.
                      (1/cmds/format.asm):00033         * Added support for formatting Dragon floppies, this is required because
                      (1/cmds/format.asm):00034         * dragon floppies are aranged thus :-
                      (1/cmds/format.asm):00035         *       LSN     Purpose
                      (1/cmds/format.asm):00036         *       0       Standard LSN0
                      (1/cmds/format.asm):00037         *       1       Blockmap
                      (1/cmds/format.asm):00038         *       2-17    Boot area (as on track 35 of CoCo disk).
                      (1/cmds/format.asm):00039         *       18      Begining of root dir
                      (1/cmds/format.asm):00040         *       19+     Continuation of root dir ? and data sectors.
                      (1/cmds/format.asm):00041         *
                      (1/cmds/format.asm):00042         * Note as a limitation of this scheme, is that disks with more than 2048
                      (1/cmds/format.asm):00043         * sectors, need to have a cluster size of 2 as only one sector is available
                      (1/cmds/format.asm):00044         * for the block map.
                      (1/cmds/format.asm):00045         *
                      (1/cmds/format.asm):00046         * To format a floppy with dragon format, you need to use the command line
                      (1/cmds/format.asm):00047         * parameter 'FD' (format, Dragon).
                      (1/cmds/format.asm):00048         *
                      (1/cmds/format.asm):00049         *       2005-10-26  P.Harvey-Smith
                      (1/cmds/format.asm):00050         * Determined the purpose and commented some of the unknown memory vars,
                      (1/cmds/format.asm):00051         * also renamed others to more closeley represent their purpose, e.g.
                      (1/cmds/format.asm):00052         * there where two 'cluster size' vars, one was inface number of bytes in
                      (1/cmds/format.asm):00053         * bitmap, so that got renamed :)
                      (1/cmds/format.asm):00054         * Format can now correctly build a DragonData OS-9 compatible disk
                      (1/cmds/format.asm):00055         * that can have (under OS-9) cobbler run on it, and will subsequently then
                      (1/cmds/format.asm):00056         * boot.
                      (1/cmds/format.asm):00057         *
                      (1/cmds/format.asm):00058         *  25   2005-10-26  Boisy G. Pitre
                      (1/cmds/format.asm):00059         * Fixed an issue where the bitmap sector wasn't being properly set up
                      (1/cmds/format.asm):00060         * due to some incorrect assumptions.  The result was that copying a file
                      (1/cmds/format.asm):00061         * to a newly formatted hard drive would, in cases where the drive was
                      (1/cmds/format.asm):00062         * large, wipe out the bitmap sector and root directory area.
                      (1/cmds/format.asm):00063         *
                      (1/cmds/format.asm):00064         *       2020-01-05  David Ladd
                      (1/cmds/format.asm):00065         * Added enhanced sector data for the special 20 sector per track on
                      (1/cmds/format.asm):00066         * floppy disks.  Added new option E to allow using this enhanced
                      (1/cmds/format.asm):00067         * sector data.
                      (1/cmds/format.asm):00068         
                      (1/cmds/format.asm):00069                             nam       Format
                      (1/cmds/format.asm):00070                             ttl       RBF Disk format program
                      (1/cmds/format.asm):00071         
